        "original_id": "d1e2faf0-b127-5b62-90b6-9cf82ee30e91",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikael Åkerfeldt, Lee Ranaldo, Thurston Moore, Lunch, Steven Wilson\n- Bands/Projects: Opeth, Bloodbath, Steel, Storm Corrosion, Sonic Youth, Death Valley '69'\n- Organizations/Publications: Rolling Stone, Spin\n- Roles: musician, vocalist, guitarist, songwriter, writer, visual artist, record producer\n\nFacts:\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was born on 17 April 1974 and is a Swedish musician.\n- Lee Ranaldo was born on February 3, 1956 and is an American musician, singer-songwriter, guitarist, writer, visual artist, and record producer.\n- In 1984, Thurston Moore and fellow New York musician Lunch wrote and sang the song \"Death Valley '69,\" and Martin Bisi recorded it.\n- In 2004, Rolling Stone ranked Lee Ranaldo at number 33 on its \"Greatest Guitarists of All Time\" list.\n- In May 2012, Spin published a staff-selected top 100 ranking that placed Thurston Moore and his Sonic Youth bandmate Lee Ranaldo together at number 1.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is prominently known as the lead vocalist, guitarist, and primary songwriter of Opeth.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is the former vocalist of Bloodbath.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was also guitarist for the one-off band Steel.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is part of the collaboration Storm Corrosion with Steven Wilson.\n- Lee Ranaldo is best known as a co-founder of Sonic Youth.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
